# Rendered by paisans. Do not edit: `paisans apply` overwrites this file.
#
# Routing for auth, imported by the gateway's block for
# id.example.org.
#
# POST /api/signup/setup takes no authentication and makes its caller an
# administrator, answering with an admin session (usersignup/module.go:86-87
# at v2.14.0). It is open while Pocket ID has no user besides its static API
# key's (usersignup/service.go:220-229), which is the case from the moment a
# new deployment starts until `apply` makes the declared operators, and again
# after a restore that holds no users. Whoever reaches it first in that window
# owns the identity provider. Nothing in Pocket ID turns it off, and the
# toolkit makes its admins through the static API key, so the gateway refuses
# the route for every method, always, along with /setup and /signup/setup,
# the pages that offer the form.
#
# Each pattern ends in *, so a trailing slash or anything below is refused
# too. Caddy's path matcher compares the decoded, cleaned path case
# insensitively (MatchPath in modules/caddyhttp/matchers.go at v2.11.7), so
# /API/Signup/Setup, a doubled slash, a dot segment or an escaped letter is
# refused as well.
@setup path /api/signup/setup* /signup/setup* /setup*
respond @setup 404
#
# Every other refusal below follows the rendered configuration: a route that
# serves only a feature the configuration turns off is closed. The values are
# those the .env renders, and a setting left out takes Pocket ID's default
# (appconfig/model.go:120-175 at v2.14.0).
#
# Self signup is closed while allow_user_signups is disabled, or unset, since
# Pocket ID's default is disabled (appconfig/model.go:130). Here it is
# disabled. An account app with invites on requires disabled,
# so an invite community always gets this block; otherwise Pocket ID's own
# setting decides.
#
# With allow_user_signups disabled, Pocket ID's signup page refuses
# (frontend/src/routes/signup/+page.svelte:38-41) and its admin page offers no
# signup links (frontend/src/routes/settings/admin/users/+page.svelte:65), but
# POST /api/signup still takes a signup token an administrator made
# (usersignup/service.go:51-52, route at usersignup/module.go:85). The gateway
# closes the API route, the signup pages, and /st/, which redirects a signup
# link to /signup (frontend/src/routes/st/[token]/+page.ts). /api/signup-tokens
# stays open: it is an administrator's route.
@signup path /api/signup /api/signup/* /signup /signup/* /st/*
respond @signup 404
reverse_proxy 10.44.0.1:1411 10.44.0.2:1411 {
	# Failover across apps sites; see upstream_failover in the Caddyfile.
	import upstream_failover
	header_up X-Forwarded-Proto https
}
